casebook d-30cfr-75_1103-5-mine-co-warning-draft v1
source "D-30cfr-75.1103-5-mine-co-warning.txt" dated 2026-10-14 by "drafted by anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 from the manual; not yet approved"
note "UNAPPROVED DRAFT: written by a language model from D-30cfr-75.1103-5-mine-co-warning.txt. Every declaration below cites the sentence"
note "it came from. Check each against the manual, add what the manual does not say, then delete"
note "this note to approve. quorum studio will not build a chip image while it is here."

# manual: "When the carbon monoxide level reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level at any sensor location"
observe co_high "carbon monoxide is 10 ppm above the established ambient level at a sensor location"

# manual: "If any sensor indicates a warning"
observe sensor_warning "a sensor indicates a warning"

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
observe operator_judges_safe "the mine operator has determined the signal does not present a hazard to miners"

# manual: "If any fire detection component becomes inoperative"
observe component_inoperative "a fire detection component has become inoperative"

# manual: "any change in this information"
observe map_info_changed "the sensor locations or intended air flow direction shown on the map or schematic have changed"

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
observe map_updated "the map or schematic has been updated within 24 hours of the change"

# manual: "after the belt is stopped"
observe belt_stopped "the belt has been stopped (within the last 4 hours)"

# manual: "unless an examination for hot rollers and fire is made"
observe hot_roller_exam_made "an examination for hot rollers and fire has been made"

# manual: "When a malfunction or warning signal is received at the manned surface location"
observe signal_received_surface "a malfunction or warning signal has been received at the manned surface location"

# manual: "Upon notification of a malfunction or warning signal"
observe personnel_notified "personnel have been notified of a malfunction or warning signal"

# manual: "If the warning signal will be activated during calibration of sensors"
observe calibrating "calibration of sensors is in progress and will activate the warning signal"

# manual: "If one sensor becomes inoperative"
observe one_sensor_inoperative "exactly one fire sensor has become inoperative"

# manual: "a trained person must continuously monitor for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor"
observe sensor_point_monitored "a trained person is continuously monitoring for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor"

# manual: "If two or more adjacent sensors become inoperative"
observe adjacent_sensors_inoperative "two or more adjacent fire sensors have become inoperative"

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
observe areas_patrolled "trained persons are patrolling and continuously monitoring the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they are traveled each hour in their entirety"

# manual: "Alternatively, a trained person must be stationed at each inoperative sensor to monitor for carbon monoxide"
observe sensors_stationed "a trained person is stationed at each inoperative sensor to monitor for carbon monoxide"

# manual: "If the complete fire detection system becomes inoperative"
observe system_inoperative "the complete fire detection system has become inoperative"

# manual: "any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
observe monitor_co_high "trained persons monitoring find carbon monoxide 10 ppm above the established ambient level"

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
observe operator_knows_source_harmless "the mine operator knows the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
observe assigned_emergency_duty "the miners concerned are assigned emergency response duties"

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
excuse operator_no_hazard "operator determined the signal is not a hazard to miners" needs operator_judges_safe

# manual: "When the carbon monoxide level reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level at any sensor location, automatic fire sensor and warning device systems shall provide an effective warning signal at the following locations"
claim co_alarm_condition "carbon monoxide 10 ppm above ambient at any sensor location requires a warning signal" severity 5 needs co_high

# manual: "If any fire detection component becomes inoperative, immediate action must be taken to repair the component."
claim detection_defect "an inoperative fire detection component must be repaired" severity 4 needs component_inoperative

# manual: "If any sensor indicates a warning, the following actions must be taken"
claim warning_hazard "a sensor warning requires the listed actions, including withdrawing miners; the operator's no-hazard finding undercuts it" severity 8 needs sensor_warning

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
claim map_out_of_date "the map or schematic has not been updated after a change in its information" severity 3 needs map_info_changed

# manual: "The automatic fire sensor and warning device system shall be monitored for a period of 4 hours after the belt is stopped"
claim monitoring_due "the fire sensor and warning device system must be monitored for 4 hours after the belt is stopped" severity 3 needs belt_stopped

# manual: "unless an examination for hot rollers and fire is made"
excuse hot_roller_exam "an examination for hot rollers and fire was made, so the 4-hour monitoring is not required" needs hot_roller_exam_made

# manual: "appropriate personnel must immediately initiate an investigation to determine the cause of the malfunction or warning signal"
claim investigation_due "a notified malfunction or warning signal requires an immediate investigation into its cause" severity 4 needs personnel_notified

# manual: "If one sensor becomes inoperative, a trained person must continuously monitor for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor"
claim sensor_unmonitored "one sensor is inoperative and no trained person is monitoring carbon monoxide at it, so the belt may not continue to operate" severity 4 needs one_sensor_inoperative

# manual: "If two or more adjacent sensors become inoperative, trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
claim areas_unpatrolled "two or more adjacent sensors are inoperative and the affected areas are not being patrolled and monitored for carbon monoxide, so the belt may not continue to operate" severity 4 needs adjacent_sensors_inoperative

# manual: "If the complete fire detection system becomes inoperative, trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
claim system_unpatrolled "the complete fire detection system is inoperative and the affected areas are not being patrolled and monitored for carbon monoxide" severity 4 needs system_inoperative

# manual: "Trained persons who conduct monitoring under this section must immediately report to the surface any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
claim co_report_due "monitoring persons must immediately report to the surface carbon monoxide 10 ppm above ambient" severity 4 needs monitor_co_high

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
excuse source_known_harmless "the operator knows the carbon monoxide source is not a hazard, so no report is required" needs operator_knows_source_harmless

# manual: "All miners in the affected areas, unless assigned emergency response duties, must be immediately withdrawn to a safe location identified in the mine emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction."
claim withdrawal_due "a sensor warning requires miners in the affected areas to be withdrawn to a safe location" severity 8 needs sensor_warning

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
excuse emergency_response_duty "miners assigned emergency response duties are not withdrawn" needs assigned_emergency_duty

# manual: "When a malfunction or warning signal is received at the manned surface location, the sensors that are activated must be identified and appropriate personnel immediately notified."
claim notification_due "a received malfunction or warning signal requires the activated sensors to be identified and personnel notified" severity 4 needs signal_received_surface

# manual: "If the warning signal will be activated during calibration of sensors, personnel manning the surface location must be notified prior to and upon completion of calibration."
claim calibration_notice_due "surface personnel must be notified before and after calibration that will activate the warning signal" severity 3 needs calibrating

# manual: "Affected working sections, areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, or other areas designated in the approved emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration."
claim calibration_area_notice_due "when the warning signal will be activated during calibration, affected working sections and other designated areas must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration" severity 3 needs calibrating

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
operator_no_hazard undercuts warning_hazard

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
map_updated rebuts map_out_of_date

# manual: "unless an examination for hot rollers and fire is made"
hot_roller_exam undercuts monitoring_due

# manual: "a trained person must continuously monitor for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor"
sensor_point_monitored rebuts sensor_unmonitored

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
areas_patrolled rebuts areas_unpatrolled

# manual: "Alternatively, a trained person must be stationed at each inoperative sensor to monitor for carbon monoxide"
sensors_stationed rebuts areas_unpatrolled

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
areas_patrolled rebuts system_unpatrolled

# manual: "unless the mine operator knows that the source of the carbon monoxide does not present a hazard to miners"
source_known_harmless undercuts co_report_due

# manual: "unless assigned emergency response duties"
emergency_response_duty undercuts withdrawal_due

# manual: "unless the mine operator determines that the signal does not present a hazard to miners"
operator_no_hazard undercuts withdrawal_due

# manual: "automatic fire sensor and warning device systems shall provide an effective warning signal at the following locations"
action raise_alarm when any co_alarm_condition

# manual: "If any sensor indicates a warning"
action keep_operating idle

# manual: "immediate action must be taken to repair the component"
action repair_component when any detection_defect

# manual: "This map or schematic must be updated within 24 hours of any change in this information."
action update_map when any map_out_of_date

# manual: "shall be monitored for a period of 4 hours after the belt is stopped"
action monitor_system when any monitoring_due

# manual: "the sensors that are activated must be identified and appropriate personnel immediately notified"
action notify_personnel when any notification_due

# manual: "appropriate personnel must immediately initiate an investigation to determine the cause of the malfunction or warning signal"
action investigate_signal when any investigation_due

# manual: "Appropriate personnel must notify miners in affected working sections, in affected areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, and at other locations specified in the approved mine emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction"
action notify_miners when any warning_hazard

# manual: "personnel manning the surface location must be notified prior to and upon completion of calibration"
action notify_surface_personnel when any calibration_notice_due

# manual: "Affected working sections, areas where mechanized mining equipment is being installed or removed, or other areas designated in the approved emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction must be notified at the beginning and completion of calibration."
action notify_affected_areas when any calibration_area_notice_due

# manual: "a trained person must continuously monitor for carbon monoxide at the inoperative sensor"
action monitor_inoperative_sensor when any sensor_unmonitored

# manual: "trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
action patrol_affected_areas when any areas_unpatrolled

# manual: "If the complete fire detection system becomes inoperative, trained persons must patrol and continuously monitor the affected areas for carbon monoxide so that they will be traveled each hour in their entirety"
action patrol_complete_system when any system_unpatrolled

# manual: "Trained persons who conduct monitoring under this section must immediately report to the surface any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
action report_to_surface when any co_report_due

# manual: "All miners in the affected areas, unless assigned emergency response duties, must be immediately withdrawn to a safe location identified in the mine emergency evacuation and firefighting program of instruction."
action withdraw_miners safe when any withdrawal_due warning_hazard

# manual: "Trained persons who conduct monitoring under this section must immediately report to the surface any concentration of carbon monoxide that reaches 10 parts per million above the established ambient level"
prefer withdraw_miners over notify_miners over raise_alarm over notify_personnel over notify_affected_areas over notify_surface_personnel over investigate_signal over report_to_surface over monitor_inoperative_sensor over patrol_affected_areas over patrol_complete_system over repair_component over monitor_system over update_map over keep_operating
